title test grain mesh (standard version)
# this sim tests whether resampling between the standard frequency mesh and the
# grain frequency mesh is done correctly
#
# commands controlling continuum =========
blackbody 5e4
luminosity 37
# commands for density & abundances =========
#
hden 4
grains
# commands controlling geometry  =========
#
radius 17
# other commands for details     =========
#
stop zone 1
set dr 1
# commands controlling output    =========
#
set save prefix "func_grainmesh_standard"
save monitors ".asr"
save performance ".per"
save overview ".ovr"
# commands giving the asserts    =========
#
init "func_grainmesh.ini"
#
# func_grainmesh_standard.in 
# class function
# ========================================
# 

This sim tests if resampling the grain frequency mesh onto the regular mesh
works correctly. This is the control case using a standard main frequency mesh.
These sims below all do the same thing, except that the main frequency mesh differs:
func_grainmesh_lores.in uses a very low resolution main frequency mesh,
func_grainmesh_standard.in uses a standard resolution main frequency mesh,
func_grainmesh_hires.in uses a very high resolution main frequency mesh.
These sims should give essentially identical results (though minor differences
are expected). This is why all three sims should use identical monitors that
are contained in a special init file called func_grainmesh.ini.
